stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    [*] --> Pending : POST /biometric-update-cases — updateStatus forced to "Pending", requestedAt = now

    Pending --> In_Review : PATCH .../review {status: In_Review}
    Pending --> Approved : PATCH .../review {status: Approved} — accepted, no ordering guard
    Pending --> Rejected : PATCH .../review {status: Rejected} — accepted, no ordering guard

    In_Review --> Approved : PATCH .../review {status: Approved}
    In_Review --> Rejected : PATCH .../review {status: Rejected}

    Approved --> In_Review : PATCH .../review — accepted, the current state is never checked
    Rejected --> Approved : PATCH .../review — accepted, the current state is never checked

    note right of Pending
        The review endpoint only validates the target value against
        In_Review|Approved|Rejected (zod enum / regex); it never reads
        the current update_status, so any transition above is possible.
        FINGERPRINT cases additionally require fingerNumber (400 otherwise).
    end note

    note right of Approved
        Two stores with the same API shape:
        - configuration (canonical): MemoryStore, soft delete sets deletedAt
        - biometric mirror: MongoDB biometric_update_cases, sets
          is_active=false + deleted_at, never removes the document
    end note

    Pending --> [*] : DELETE (soft delete: deletedAt / is_active=false)
    In_Review --> [*] : DELETE (soft delete)
    Approved --> [*] : DELETE (soft delete)
    Rejected --> [*] : DELETE (soft delete)
